        <mxCell id="5hhh_01M-dDIdeUSxM5c-2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#b0e3e6;strokeColor=#0e8088;sketch=1;curveFitting=1;jiggle=2;align=left;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Georgia&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 70px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;HyDE means Hypothetical Document Embeddings.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Georgia&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 70px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Georgia&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 70px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Instead of embedding the user query directly, HyDE asks the LLM to generate a hypothetical answer or passage. Then that hypothetical passage is embedded and used for retrieval. The HyDE paper explains that the generated document may be unreal or contain false details, but its embedding helps locate similar real documents in the corpus.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
